perf/openlinker-throughput/stand-ids.env
perf/openlinker-throughput/stand-bootstrap-undo.txt
# Generated by perf/openlinker-throughput's scenario scripts - one directory
# per run, per README "The results contract".
#
# SPLIT BY ROLE rather than ignored wholesale (#3009) - a deliberate departure
# from the perf/prestashop-baseline precedent this block used to follow.
# Measured on a 39-run tree: the provenance core is 130 KB across 84 files, the
# bulk 302 MB across 149, a ratio of about 2300:1. The bulk stays out -
# pool.json is generated INPUT, regenerable from its own `meta` block (205 MB
# of the 304 MB), and timeseries.csv is dominated by a docker_stats_json column
# dumping every container on the measuring workstation. The core is committed,
# because it is what says whether a figure may be quoted: the build under test,
# the guard record, the verdict, and the k6 summary's own saturation counters.
#
# The `/**` form plus the `!.../**/` line is required rather than stylistic:
# git cannot re-include a path whose PARENT DIRECTORY was excluded, so the old
# directory-only `results/` pattern made every negation below unreachable.
# See README "Evidence and artefact retention" for what this does and does not
# cover, and for the state of the back catalogue.
perf/openlinker-throughput/results/**
!perf/openlinker-throughput/results/**/
!perf/openlinker-throughput/results/**/manifest.json
!perf/openlinker-throughput/results/**/verdict.txt
!perf/openlinker-throughput/results/**/summary.json
!perf/openlinker-throughput/results/**/k6-summary.json
!perf/openlinker-throughput/results/**/pg-deadlocks.json
!perf/openlinker-throughput/results/**/*.md

# Lighthouse CI (#2866) — the committed artefact is scripts/lighthouse/baseline.json;
# a per-run report is ephemeral local/CI output.
scripts/lighthouse/last-run.json
scripts/lighthouse/.tmp-*.json
